Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; Turn off Fast Startup, so shutting down really shuts down.
; With it on, shutdown hibernates the kernel and leaves the Windows volume
; marked in use, which the Linux installs on the same disk must not write to.
; See os/windows/README.md for why.

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\Session Manager\Power]
"HiberbootEnabled"=dword:00000000
